Interpretation
  Abstract Delsarte feasibility is not unique: degrees 2,3,4 have
  3,3,5 feasible root-polynomial certificates respectively.
  The generated AP occupancy law selects exactly the THM-534 dual
  root set at every binding k=8..13.  Thus the missing lemma is not
  a sparse Tanner lemma; it is a generated-depth selection lemma.
  The parity chain selected by AP is
    K8 roots  (1,2,4,5): even Krawtchouk support K0,K2,K4
    K9 roots  (2,3,6):   mixed support K0,K1,K2,K3
    K11 roots (3,4):     mixed support K0,K1,K2
  This is the concrete puncture/extend target suggested by HYP-2740.
